1
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:13,040
This is part one of a three-part module describing an approach to interpretation of abdominal and pelvic CTs.

2
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:22,580
Following completion of all three modules, you should be able to employ a systematic search pattern when interpreting abdominal and pelvic CTs.

3
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:32,400
In this particular module, you should be able to employ a search pattern specifically for evaluation of the abdominal organs

4
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:39,680
and be able to identify alterations in the normal appearance of the abdominal organs.

5
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:47,840
A thorough evaluation for an abdominal and pelvic CT includes evaluation of the abdominal organs,

6
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:57,460
bowel and mesentery, peritoneal cavity and retroperitoneum, vessels and lymph nodes, pelvic organs, and body wall and bones.

7
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:02,720
In this module, we will specifically discuss assessment of the abdominal organs.

8
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:11,560
Take a minute to read through this example normal dictation discussing findings in the abdominal organs.

9
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:21,800
In general, when assessing the abdominal organs, one should evaluate the location, size, morphology, and contour,

10
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:27,800
as well as the attenuation and or enhancement of the organ.

11
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:35,320
Now, enhancement can include global or overall enhancement, which is often an indicator of vascular supply,

12
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:42,540
or focal enhancing abnormalities, such as masses, scars, or infarcts.

13
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:49,440
Now, let's get into discussion of each individual abdominal organ.

14
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:56,200
Assessment of the liver should begin with an overall evaluation of morphology and attenuation.

15
00:01:57,340 --> 00:02:05,540
The normal liver attenuation is equal to or greater than the spleen on both contrast and non-contrast images.

16
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:14,660
In this example, we have a non-contrast CT showing a liver attenuation slightly more than that of the spleen.

17
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:27,060
To assess for steatosis on CT, on a non-contrast image, if the liver attenuation is more than 10 Hounsfield units less than that of the spleen,

18
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:31,300
that's consistent with steatosis.

19
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:40,400
On the portal venous phase, the liver attenuation should be somewhere between 20 and 30 Hounsfield units less than the spleen.

20
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:47,020
There are different patterns of steatosis within the liver.

21
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:53,300
On the previous slide, I showed you two examples of kind of uniform diffuse steatosis.

22
00:02:54,380 --> 00:03:03,580
Steatosis can also be multifocal or focal, both focal infiltration where there's fat or focal areas of sparing.

23
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:13,480
The image on the left shows diffuse severe hepatic steatosis, while the image on the right shows inhomogeneous steatosis.

24
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:21,140
As you can see, the right hepatic lobe is more affected than the normally enhancing left hepatic lobe.

25
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:28,170
How can you confidently make the diagnosis of focal fat deposition or sparing?

26
00:03:28,170 --> 00:03:35,490
Well, this is more definitively evaluated with MRI, although that's beyond the scope of this discussion.

27
00:03:36,790 --> 00:03:46,810
Characteristic imaging findings for focal fat deposition or areas of sparing within the liver include the location of the abnormality,

28
00:03:47,450 --> 00:03:49,070
the margin of the abnormality.

29
00:03:49,070 --> 00:03:59,530
So, fat deposition typically has straight or geographic margins as opposed to curved margins of masses, such as neoplasms, which tend to be round or oval.

30
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:05,350
And finally, fat deposition or sparing tends to lack mass effect.

31
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:15,150
So, in this example, notice the focal low attenuation in the lateral segment of the left hepatic lobe with a straight ventral margin.

32
00:04:15,150 --> 00:04:20,690
And notice that there are some vessels coursing through this that are not displaced.

33
00:04:20,910 --> 00:04:24,430
So, these findings are suggestive of focal fat deposition.

34
00:04:25,150 --> 00:04:34,730
Here, it's deposition of fat because the attenuation is lower than that of the surrounding normally enhancing hepatic parenchyma.

35
00:04:34,730 --> 00:04:53,290
What are the characteristic locations for focal fat sparing or focal fat deposition adjacent to the falciform ligament around the portahepidus and around the gallbladder fossa?

36
00:04:53,390 --> 00:04:55,150
These are the characteristic locations.

37
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:59,090
Now, these are normal images, so there's no focal fat deposition present here,

38
00:04:59,170 --> 00:05:04,870
but these are the characteristic locations at which you typically see this finding.

39
00:05:04,870 --> 00:05:12,790
In addition to evaluating for the presence of steatosis, if intravenous contrast material is administered,

40
00:05:13,370 --> 00:05:16,910
you want to assess overall enhancement of the organ.

41
00:05:17,570 --> 00:05:21,150
If there is a global abnormality in enhancement of the liver,

42
00:05:21,890 --> 00:05:28,030
you should think of abnormalities of either blood flow in, which is typically portal vein thrombosis,

43
00:05:28,030 --> 00:05:35,710
or blood flow out, which may reflect thrombosis of the hepatic veins or small hepatic venules,

44
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:38,130
or passive hepatic congestion.

45
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:43,670
In this example, notice the diffuse heterogeneous enhancement of the liver.

46
00:05:44,290 --> 00:05:51,370
This is a case of passive congestion of the liver from a patient with right heart failure.

47
00:05:51,370 --> 00:06:01,460
In addition to evaluating hepatic attenuation and enhancement, you also need to assess overall hepatic morphology.

48
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:06,480
This specifically means evaluating for the presence or absence of cirrhosis.

49
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:13,420
Now, cirrhosis manifests itself as abnormalities of hepatic volume and surface contour.

50
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:19,220
Classically, the cirrhotic liver becomes atrophic.

51
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:24,280
However, the degree to which different segments are affected varies,

52
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:31,200
and this often leads to a volume redistribution, often termed atrophy-hypertrophy complex.

53
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:39,560
Now, a classic configuration of this is that the caudate lobe and the lateral segment of the left lobe

54
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:45,680
typically become relatively hypertrophic compared to the right lobe,

55
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:49,380
which is more affected and becomes atrophic.

56
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:54,040
So, this is termed atrophy-hypertrophy complex or volume distribution.

57
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:59,660
Atrophy, in general, within the liver manifests itself in a couple of ways.

58
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:03,600
So, one of the things that you'll see as the parenchymus shrinks down

59
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:09,380
is that the fissures will widen, as shown on the image on the left.

60
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:16,080
In addition, notice the increase in periportal space.

61
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:21,300
In other words, the fat within the periportal space, that is, between the portal vein

62
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:25,160
and the adjacent hepatic parenchyma increases.

63
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:27,620
So, you get an enlarged periportal space.

64
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:30,240
So, basically, as the liver volume shrinks,

65
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:33,500
the fissures in the periportal space become more evident.

66
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:40,440
In addition, as the liver tries to regenerate itself from the insult,

67
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:42,720
it does so in a nodular pattern,

68
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,840
which on the surface of the liver can manifest itself.

69
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:50,060
A surface contour nodularity, as shown on the image on the right.

70
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,320
If cirrhosis is identified,

71
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:58,060
you need to look for sequelae of portal hypertension,

72
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:03,560
which includes formation of portosystemic collateral vessels, or varices,

73
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,560
an enlarged spleen, ascites,

74
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:10,540
or increased in size of the portal vein with a ruffle of thumb

75
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:14,000
of greater than 13 millimeters in diameter.

76
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:18,600
In this image, in a patient with cirrhosis and portal hypertension,

77
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:22,520
we can identify an enlarged spleen, or spleenomegaly,

78
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:26,120
as well as portosystemic collateral vessels,

79
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:29,660
in this case, perigastric collateral vessels.

80
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:39,640
This question tests your knowledge of the characteristic imaging findings

81
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,980
for focal fat deposition or sparing.

82
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:48,400
This includes geographic margins, so straight margins,

83
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,380
lack of mass effect.

84
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:53,240
Remember, these occur in characteristic locations,

85
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:59,020
and will have different attenuation as compared to the background liver.

86
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:01,260
In the case of focal fat deposition,

87
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:04,680
this will be lower in attenuation than the background parenchyma

88
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:05,780
as shown in this image.

89
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:08,740
In the case of focal fatty sparing,

90
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:14,420
the focal abnormality will be high in attenuation

91
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:16,940
because it is spared from fat deposition

92
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:19,120
when compared to the background liver.

93
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:24,230
We'll now move on to evaluation of the bile ducts.

94
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:27,170
So that would include assessment of both the intra-hepatic ducts

95
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:28,350
and extra-hepatic duct.

96
00:09:28,870 --> 00:09:34,650
In this case, you see these branching low attenuation abnormalities

97
00:09:34,650 --> 00:09:36,730
adjacent to the portal vein branches.

98
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:41,090
This is the appearance of bile duct dilatation on CT.

99
00:09:41,090 --> 00:09:46,310
You must be careful to distinguish true bile duct dilatation

100
00:09:46,310 --> 00:09:47,730
from periportal edema.

101
00:09:48,570 --> 00:09:53,670
Bile duct dilatation will appear as linear and branching abnormality

102
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:59,410
that's low attenuation, but only on one side of the portal vein branch

103
00:09:59,410 --> 00:10:01,450
as shown on the image on the left.

104
00:10:01,450 --> 00:10:05,210
In the image on the right, there is low attenuation

105
00:10:05,210 --> 00:10:08,570
surrounding the portal vein branch

106
00:10:08,570 --> 00:10:11,210
that is on both sides of the portal vein branch,

107
00:10:11,470 --> 00:10:13,910
and that's consistent with periportal edema.

108
00:10:14,970 --> 00:10:18,530
If you identify gas within the liver,

109
00:10:20,250 --> 00:10:22,390
particularly in branching structures,

110
00:10:22,910 --> 00:10:26,550
the typical differential diagnosis will include pneumobilia,

111
00:10:26,550 --> 00:10:30,330
that is gas within the bile ducts

112
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:34,210
versus gas within the portal venous system.

113
00:10:35,150 --> 00:10:38,270
Pneumobilia tends to be central in location

114
00:10:38,270 --> 00:10:41,670
because the bile flow is towards the hilum.

115
00:10:42,630 --> 00:10:45,970
You often identify an adjacent opacified portal vein

116
00:10:45,970 --> 00:10:48,390
in the case of the contrast-enhanced CT.

117
00:10:49,450 --> 00:10:51,610
Portal venous gas tends to be peripheral,

118
00:10:51,970 --> 00:10:53,730
and this central versus peripheral rule

119
00:10:53,730 --> 00:10:55,470
was originally described as,

120
00:10:55,470 --> 00:10:57,290
in terms of radiography

121
00:10:57,290 --> 00:10:59,550
and may be less applicable to CT,

122
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:00,950
but you will still hear people

123
00:11:00,950 --> 00:11:02,710
kind of talk about this rule.

124
00:11:04,010 --> 00:11:09,970
So, because of the flow of the portal vein

125
00:11:09,970 --> 00:11:11,210
towards the periphery of the liver,

126
00:11:11,310 --> 00:11:15,510
the gas tends to be pushed out to the periphery,

127
00:11:15,770 --> 00:11:17,650
and also you should notice

128
00:11:17,650 --> 00:11:21,350
no adjacent opacified portal vein

129
00:11:21,350 --> 00:11:25,210
since the gas is within the portal vein itself.

130
00:11:25,470 --> 00:11:29,610
When evaluating the gallbladder on CT,

131
00:11:30,510 --> 00:11:33,930
you want to assess both the wall and the lumen.

132
00:11:34,670 --> 00:11:35,970
In terms of the wall,

133
00:11:36,050 --> 00:11:39,570
you want to evaluate wall thickness and enhancement,

134
00:11:40,290 --> 00:11:43,250
provided that intravenous contrast material has been given.

135
00:11:43,730 --> 00:11:45,530
When assessing the lumen,

136
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:48,810
you need to evaluate overall luminal attenuation

137
00:11:48,810 --> 00:11:51,330
as well as for masses or gallstones.

138
00:11:51,630 --> 00:11:58,010
This is a coronal CT image that shows a normal gallbladder

139
00:11:58,010 --> 00:12:00,290
with normal luminal attenuation

140
00:12:00,290 --> 00:12:02,850
and normal wall thickness and enhancement.

141
00:12:02,850 --> 00:12:08,270
These are two examples of abnormal gallbladder walls.

142
00:12:08,390 --> 00:12:10,670
The image on the left shows a thickened

143
00:12:10,670 --> 00:12:12,710
and heterogeneously enhancing wall

144
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:13,950
with adjacent inflammation,

145
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:18,650
while the image on the right shows an irregular wall

146
00:12:18,650 --> 00:12:21,990
with apparent interruptions of the mucosal surface.

147
00:12:21,990 --> 00:12:27,460
CT is less sensitive for detection of gallstones

148
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:30,780
as compared to ultrasound or MRI,

149
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:34,300
although gallstones may be visible on CT,

150
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:37,060
particularly if they're calcified or contained gas.

151
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:40,400
The image on the left is a non-contrast CT

152
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:44,820
showing multiple small calcified gallstones

153
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:46,260
in the dependent gallbladder

154
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:49,220
with probably a little bit of sludge adjacent to that.

155
00:12:49,220 --> 00:12:52,500
The image on the right shows larger

156
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,200
peripherally calcified gallstones

157
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,760
containing nitrogen gas.

158
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:59,340
So that's gas within the gallstone,

159
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:01,420
which is a normal finding

160
00:13:01,420 --> 00:13:04,520
or at least nothing to be concerned about.

161
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:07,200
That's as opposed to gas within the gallbladder lumen

162
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,840
or gas within the gallbladder wall.

163
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:11,320
So if you see gas within the gallbladder wall,

164
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:12,640
then you want to be thinking about

165
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:14,220
emphysematous cholecystitis.

166
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:17,300
Here are three examples

167
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:19,320
of abnormal luminal attenuation.

168
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:20,560
The image on the left

169
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:25,140
we previously described as being gallstones

170
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:27,380
as well as some gallbladder sludge.

171
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:28,940
The image in the middle

172
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:32,740
shows more mass-like high attenuation

173
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:34,360
relative to the background bile,

174
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:35,980
which turned out to be tumerfactive

175
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:37,280
or mass-like sludge.

176
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:39,300
And then the image on the right

177
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:41,600
actually shows an enhancing mass

178
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:43,840
within the gallbladder lumen.

179
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:51,890
This question tests your ability

180
00:13:51,890 --> 00:13:53,530
to distinguish pneumobilia

181
00:13:53,530 --> 00:13:54,890
from portal venous gas.

182
00:13:55,750 --> 00:13:58,190
In this case, we are dealing with pneumobilia,

183
00:13:58,590 --> 00:14:01,110
which manifests itself as gas attenuation

184
00:14:01,110 --> 00:14:03,650
within the bile ducts.

185
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:05,570
You can distinguish this

186
00:14:05,570 --> 00:14:07,610
from portal vein gas

187
00:14:07,610 --> 00:14:09,930
by the presence of an enhancing portal vein

188
00:14:09,930 --> 00:14:12,050
adjacent to the gas-containing

189
00:14:12,050 --> 00:14:13,690
structure of interest.

190
00:14:13,870 --> 00:14:16,090
So we know that this must be in the bile duct

191
00:14:16,090 --> 00:14:18,230
and not the portal vein.

192
00:14:20,210 --> 00:14:21,970
Evaluation of the spleen

193
00:14:21,970 --> 00:14:23,430
should begin with an assessment

194
00:14:23,430 --> 00:14:25,050
of overall spleen size.

195
00:14:25,850 --> 00:14:27,150
As a rule of thumb,

196
00:14:27,590 --> 00:14:29,210
you can measure the spleen

197
00:14:29,210 --> 00:14:31,210
in the cranial caudal dimension

198
00:14:31,210 --> 00:14:32,430
on a coronal image.

199
00:14:33,230 --> 00:14:34,290
A spleen that measures

200
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:38,090
more than 13 or 14 centimeters in length

201
00:14:38,090 --> 00:14:41,190
as shown on this coronal T2-weighted MR sequence

202
00:14:41,190 --> 00:14:43,850
is considered enlarged.

203
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,960
Often when evaluating the spleen,

204
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:50,960
you will identify adjacent masses

205
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:53,580
that are often round with smooth margins

206
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:55,840
and show imaging characteristics

207
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:59,720
similar to that of the adjacent spleen.

208
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:04,120
These are typically normal congenital findings

209
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,320
termed splenules,

210
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:07,320
which basically represent

211
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:10,320
a focus of splenic parenchyma

212
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:12,300
or a splenic island that failed

213
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:15,900
to coalesce with the larger spleen

214
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:16,720
during development.

215
00:15:16,980 --> 00:15:18,280
So these are normal findings.

216
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:19,820
Although they can be affected

217
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,180
by the same splenic processes

218
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:26,900
that the dominant spleen is involved with.

219
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:30,020
Evaluation of splenic enhancement

220
00:15:30,020 --> 00:15:32,340
can be tricky for those

221
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:36,120
that are new to CT evaluation.

222
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:38,140
There is differential flow

223
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:40,360
between the red and white pulp

224
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:41,060
of the spleen,

225
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:43,720
which often manifests itself

226
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:47,580
as a striped appearance

227
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:49,520
on arterial phase images.

228
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:52,540
So early images will have this appearance

229
00:15:52,540 --> 00:15:54,860
often termed a tiger spleen

230
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:56,160
given its striped appearance.

231
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:58,480
You can see that on both CT

232
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,700
on the image on the left

233
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:00,200
and MRI

234
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:03,580
with the image on the right.

235
00:16:03,580 --> 00:16:04,720
The key here

236
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,900
is that this normalizes with time.

237
00:16:07,020 --> 00:16:07,540
So if you wait

238
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:08,940
to the portal venous phase,

239
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:11,420
the spleen will show

240
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:14,500
its normal homogeneous enhancement.

241
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:15,560
So just beware

242
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:17,680
that this is not an abnormal finding.

243
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,920
Assessment of the pancreas

244
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:21,820
includes evaluation

245
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:23,580
for enhancement mass

246
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,460
as well as assessment

247
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:26,960
of the pancreatic duct

248
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,220
in terms of its caliber

249
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:29,480
and the presence

250
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:30,980
of any ductal variance,

251
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:33,240
particularly pancreatic divism.

252
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:35,540
This is an example

253
00:16:35,540 --> 00:16:37,740
of necrotizing pancreatitis,

254
00:16:37,860 --> 00:16:39,680
which shows abnormal enhancement

255
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:40,560
of the pancreas.

256
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:42,980
Notice the normal enhancing

257
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:46,640
parenchyma of the pancreatic head

258
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,440
as compared to regions

259
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,640
of non-enhancement

260
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:51,040
in the pancreatic body

261
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:53,640
secondary to necrotizing pancreatitis.

262
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:56,120
Here are two examples

263
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,240
of abnormalities

264
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:58,860
of the pancreatic duct.

265
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:00,780
The image on the left

266
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:02,920
shows dilatation

267
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:04,980
of both the common bile duct

268
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:07,240
as well as the pancreatic duct.

269
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,120
So this is a double duct sign

270
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:12,740
secondary to an ampullary mass,

271
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,680
which is not well visualized

272
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:15,440
on this image.

273
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:17,700
The image on the right

274
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:21,400
shows a calcific attenuation

275
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:25,140
focus in the pancreatic duct

276
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:27,060
consistent with a pancreatic duct

277
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:28,600
calculus.

278
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:31,920
Evaluation of the kidney

279
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,180
should include assessment

280
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:34,440
of overall size.

281
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:36,240
A rough rule of thumb

282
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,580
is that the kidney

283
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:38,340
should measure

284
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:41,000
9 to 13 millimeters

285
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,040
in cranial caudal length.

286
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,620
You should evaluate

287
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:47,200
renal position enhancement.

288
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:48,420
And given that there are

289
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:49,060
two kidneys,

290
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:52,620
you have the additional need

291
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:54,320
to assess for symmetry

292
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:55,260
of enhancement.

293
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:56,940
Not only the uniformity

294
00:17:56,940 --> 00:17:57,740
of a given kidney,

295
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:59,440
but also the symmetry

296
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:01,120
of enhancement and excretion

297
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,620
if delayed images

298
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:03,240
are performed.

299
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:04,420
And then finally,

300
00:18:04,540 --> 00:18:05,300
you want to evaluate

301
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:06,600
for collecting system

302
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:09,140
dilatation or calculi.

303
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:11,580
This is an example

304
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:13,560
of abnormal renal position

305
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:16,100
termed crostectopia.

306
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:17,720
In this case,

307
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,820
both kidneys are located

308
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:20,040
on the same side,

309
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,200
but because the ureter

310
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,760
from one of these kidneys

311
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,120
must cross the midline

312
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,640
to insert into the bladder,

313
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:28,020
this is called

314
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:29,120
a crostectopia.

315
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:32,240
So in this patient,

316
00:18:32,420 --> 00:18:33,880
we have the left kidney,

317
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:35,140
which is normally located

318
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:35,820
on the left.

319
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:37,800
The right kidney, however,

320
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:38,880
is also located

321
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,960
on the left,

322
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,220
but notice how that ureter

323
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:42,540
has to cross the midline

324
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:44,880
to insert into the right

325
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,720
ureterovesical junction.

326
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,400
That's termed crostectopia.

327
00:18:49,980 --> 00:18:51,640
Notice on the sagittal image

328
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:52,880
that the renal parenchyma

329
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,020
from the right and left kidney

330
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:55,660
are fused,

331
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:57,880
and that's why this is termed

332
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,660
a crost-fused ectopia.

333
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:03,160
This is another example

334
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,700
of abnormal renal position

335
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:07,360
secondary to an abnormality

336
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,000
of fusion.

337
00:19:08,540 --> 00:19:10,640
This is termed a horseshoe kidney

338
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:13,040
and results from midline fusion

339
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:13,720
of the kidneys,

340
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:15,200
often at the level

341
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:17,920
of the inferior mesenteric artery.

342
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:19,360
So on the coronal image

343
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:21,380
on the left,

344
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:23,320
we can see fusion.

345
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:26,000
So this area that connects the two

346
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,200
is termed the isthmus.

347
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:28,000
In this case,

348
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:30,980
it's normal renal cortex,

349
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:32,520
but may just simply be

350
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:33,660
a fibrous band.

351
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:34,660
That'll vary

352
00:19:34,660 --> 00:19:38,140
depending on the individual patient.

353
00:19:38,940 --> 00:19:39,860
On the axial image,

354
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:41,720
you see a similar finding

355
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:43,320
with midline fusion,

356
00:19:43,900 --> 00:19:45,940
often just below the level

357
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:47,980
of the inferior mesenteric artery.

358
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:50,600
The kidneys should enhance

359
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:52,840
uniformly and symmetrically,

360
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:54,440
and we've previously talked

361
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:56,340
about the different phases

362
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:57,460
of renal enhancement,

363
00:19:57,660 --> 00:19:59,680
including the corticomedullary phase,

364
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:01,880
followed by the nephrographic phase,

365
00:20:01,980 --> 00:20:03,400
followed by the excretory

366
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:04,660
or urographic stage.

367
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:06,920
If you see a delay

368
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:10,020
in a nephrogram or excretion,

369
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:11,940
you want to think of three things.

370
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:12,800
Either there's a problem

371
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,080
with blood coming in,

372
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:16,620
blood flowing out,

373
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:18,380
or urine getting out.

374
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:19,860
So we're either talking about

375
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:20,860
some abnormality

376
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:22,100
of the renal artery,

377
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:23,200
renal vein,

378
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:26,340
or collecting system obstruction.

379
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,340
So notice on the image

380
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:29,400
on the left,

381
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:32,160
there is a delayed nephrogram

382
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:34,280
of the right kidney,

383
00:20:34,340 --> 00:20:34,820
which is still

384
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:36,400
in the corticomedullary phase

385
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,220
when the left kidney

386
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:39,420
is in a nephrographic phase.

387
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:43,640
We can see how that persists

388
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:45,860
with delayed phase images

389
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:46,840
where the left kidney

390
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:48,520
is in the excretory phase

391
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,160
and the right kidney

392
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:51,080
is delayed

393
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:51,940
and is only

394
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:53,380
in the nephrographic phase.

395
00:20:55,990 --> 00:20:56,910
Renal stone evaluation

396
00:20:56,910 --> 00:20:58,090
is fairly straightforward

397
00:20:58,090 --> 00:20:58,990
on CT.

398
00:20:59,390 --> 00:21:00,570
This is probably best done

399
00:21:00,570 --> 00:21:02,030
with non-contrast CT,

400
00:21:02,290 --> 00:21:03,730
so you're not fooled

401
00:21:03,730 --> 00:21:04,430
by the presence

402
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:05,710
of contrast mimicking

403
00:21:05,710 --> 00:21:06,250
a stone

404
00:21:06,250 --> 00:21:07,750
in the early

405
00:21:07,750 --> 00:21:09,870
excretory phase.

406
00:21:10,410 --> 00:21:12,270
Nearly all renal calculi

407
00:21:12,270 --> 00:21:13,050
will be visible

408
00:21:13,050 --> 00:21:14,350
and high in attenuation

409
00:21:14,350 --> 00:21:16,690
even if they're not calcified.

410
00:21:17,390 --> 00:21:19,170
There are very few exceptions.

411
00:21:19,390 --> 00:21:20,850
Kind of a classic exception

412
00:21:20,850 --> 00:21:21,550
is a stone

413
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:22,750
that's related

414
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:25,090
to the protease inhibitors.

415
00:21:26,150 --> 00:21:27,150
But for the most part,

416
00:21:27,650 --> 00:21:28,590
stones will be visible

417
00:21:28,590 --> 00:21:29,750
and high in attenuation

418
00:21:29,750 --> 00:21:30,630
regardless if they're

419
00:21:30,630 --> 00:21:31,590
calcified or not.

420
00:21:32,090 --> 00:21:33,110
Here are two examples.

421
00:21:33,230 --> 00:21:35,270
A right renal calculus here

422
00:21:35,270 --> 00:21:36,610
on the image on the left

423
00:21:36,610 --> 00:21:37,830
and the coronal image

424
00:21:37,830 --> 00:21:39,130
showing a non-obstructing

425
00:21:39,130 --> 00:21:40,270
right lower pole

426
00:21:40,270 --> 00:21:41,050
renal calculus.

427
00:21:41,050 --> 00:21:43,810
You also need to identify

428
00:21:43,810 --> 00:21:44,930
the presence or absence

429
00:21:44,930 --> 00:21:46,790
of collecting system dilatation.

430
00:21:47,490 --> 00:21:48,770
Collecting system dilatation

431
00:21:48,770 --> 00:21:49,850
will manifest itself

432
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,370
as an increase in size

433
00:21:51,370 --> 00:21:52,650
of the collecting system

434
00:21:52,650 --> 00:21:54,090
with effacement

435
00:21:54,090 --> 00:21:55,790
of the renal sinus fat.

436
00:21:56,750 --> 00:21:58,330
The image on the right

437
00:21:58,330 --> 00:22:00,010
shows fluid attenuation,

438
00:22:00,730 --> 00:22:02,630
branching, connecting structures

439
00:22:02,630 --> 00:22:03,910
in the renal sinus

440
00:22:03,910 --> 00:22:05,750
consistent with a dilated

441
00:22:05,750 --> 00:22:06,770
collecting system.

442
00:22:07,050 --> 00:22:08,890
This is on both sides.

443
00:22:08,890 --> 00:22:11,030
This is bilateral collecting

444
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:12,130
system dilatation.

445
00:22:12,650 --> 00:22:14,830
The image on the right

446
00:22:14,830 --> 00:22:17,310
shows unilateral right-sided

447
00:22:17,310 --> 00:22:19,070
collecting system dilatation

448
00:22:19,070 --> 00:22:22,230
with edema and inflammation

449
00:22:22,230 --> 00:22:24,150
in the adjacent perinephric.

450
00:22:24,570 --> 00:22:25,090
Fat.

451
00:22:25,450 --> 00:22:27,970
If you compare the renal sinus fat

452
00:22:27,970 --> 00:22:30,050
of the right kidney

453
00:22:30,050 --> 00:22:31,190
versus the left kidney,

454
00:22:31,750 --> 00:22:32,610
you'll notice that

455
00:22:32,610 --> 00:22:35,930
you can more easily identify

456
00:22:35,930 --> 00:22:37,250
the renal sinus fat

457
00:22:37,250 --> 00:22:38,690
on the left is shown here.

458
00:22:39,810 --> 00:22:42,470
So assessment for symmetry

459
00:22:42,470 --> 00:22:43,530
of the renal sinus fat

460
00:22:43,530 --> 00:22:44,590
can help you identify

461
00:22:44,590 --> 00:22:47,150
subtle collecting system dilatation

462
00:22:47,150 --> 00:22:48,670
and we'll see an example of that

463
00:22:48,670 --> 00:22:50,390
on the next slide.

464
00:22:51,530 --> 00:22:52,910
So sometimes collecting

465
00:22:52,910 --> 00:22:53,910
system dilatation

466
00:22:53,910 --> 00:22:54,810
can be more subtle

467
00:22:54,810 --> 00:22:55,470
than present

468
00:22:55,470 --> 00:22:57,670
on the examples

469
00:22:57,670 --> 00:22:58,710
in the prior slide

470
00:22:58,710 --> 00:23:00,310
and you can actually use

471
00:23:00,310 --> 00:23:01,670
the renal sinus fat

472
00:23:01,670 --> 00:23:03,470
to help detect

473
00:23:03,470 --> 00:23:05,930
subtle collecting system dilatation.

474
00:23:05,930 --> 00:23:07,510
So if we compare

475
00:23:07,510 --> 00:23:08,390
in this example

476
00:23:08,390 --> 00:23:09,910
the right and left

477
00:23:09,910 --> 00:23:11,690
renal sinuses,

478
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:13,690
notice on the right side

479
00:23:13,690 --> 00:23:15,050
we see less

480
00:23:15,050 --> 00:23:16,670
renal sinus fat

481
00:23:16,670 --> 00:23:17,850
and that's because

482
00:23:17,850 --> 00:23:19,010
there's a dilated

483
00:23:19,010 --> 00:23:20,330
intrarenal collecting system

484
00:23:20,330 --> 00:23:21,770
that kind of effaces

485
00:23:21,770 --> 00:23:22,450
that fat.

486
00:23:22,990 --> 00:23:23,950
The image on the right

487
00:23:23,950 --> 00:23:25,770
shows normal renal sinus

488
00:23:25,770 --> 00:23:28,590
fat because it is not

489
00:23:28,590 --> 00:23:30,410
effaced by dilated

490
00:23:30,410 --> 00:23:31,390
collecting system.

491
00:23:34,320 --> 00:23:35,200
The adrenal glands

492
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:36,660
should be evaluated

493
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:37,960
for morphology,

494
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:39,480
symmetry,

495
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:41,000
thickness,

496
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:42,200
and most importantly

497
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:43,040
for the presence

498
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:45,320
of a nodule.

499
00:23:45,580 --> 00:23:47,140
A general rule of thumb

500
00:23:47,140 --> 00:23:48,540
for thickness

501
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:50,220
of an adrenal limb

502
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:50,660
and remember

503
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:51,500
the adrenal glands

504
00:23:51,500 --> 00:23:52,120
are going to be

505
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:53,800
either inverted Y

506
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:55,240
shaped or inverted

507
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:55,900
V shaped

508
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:56,540
in terms of their

509
00:23:56,540 --> 00:23:57,160
morphology.

510
00:23:58,160 --> 00:23:59,120
If a given limb

511
00:23:59,120 --> 00:23:59,740
is more than

512
00:23:59,740 --> 00:24:01,000
10 millimeters thick

513
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,080
this may be

514
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:03,240
considered abnormal.

515
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:06,180
A full discussion

516
00:24:06,180 --> 00:24:06,840
of the workup

517
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:07,700
of adrenal nodules

518
00:24:07,700 --> 00:24:08,960
is beyond the scope

519
00:24:08,960 --> 00:24:11,260
of this module.

520
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:12,080
I just want you

521
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:12,660
to be aware

522
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:13,260
at this point

523
00:24:13,260 --> 00:24:14,760
that the primary

524
00:24:14,760 --> 00:24:15,540
abnormality

525
00:24:15,540 --> 00:24:15,960
that you're going

526
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:16,700
to identify

527
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:18,360
in adrenal glands

528
00:24:18,360 --> 00:24:19,080
is the presence

529
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:19,740
or absence

530
00:24:19,740 --> 00:24:20,700
of a nodule.

531
00:24:20,780 --> 00:24:21,460
That's the main thing

532
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:21,880
that you're going

533
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:24,140
to have to evaluate.

534
00:24:24,500 --> 00:24:25,380
The vast majority

535
00:24:25,380 --> 00:24:26,320
of adrenal nodules

536
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:27,200
are going to be

537
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,380
benign adenomas.

538
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:29,480
On imaging

539
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:30,540
you can't determine

540
00:24:30,540 --> 00:24:31,520
whether or not

541
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:32,280
that's a functioning

542
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:33,060
abnormality

543
00:24:33,060 --> 00:24:33,960
and there's a debate

544
00:24:33,960 --> 00:24:34,740
on whether or not

545
00:24:34,740 --> 00:24:35,440
every patient

546
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:36,740
with a detectable

547
00:24:36,740 --> 00:24:37,700
nodule actually

548
00:24:37,700 --> 00:24:38,660
needs a biochemical

549
00:24:38,660 --> 00:24:40,820
evaluation to assess

550
00:24:40,820 --> 00:24:41,780
for whether or not

551
00:24:41,780 --> 00:24:42,360
that nodule

552
00:24:42,360 --> 00:24:44,060
is functioning or not.

553
00:24:44,380 --> 00:24:45,560
This is an example

554
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:47,300
of a right adrenal

555
00:24:47,300 --> 00:24:48,280
nodule

556
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:49,120
that's shown here.

557
00:24:57,280 --> 00:24:57,860
This question

558
00:24:57,860 --> 00:24:58,720
tests your knowledge

559
00:24:58,720 --> 00:24:59,840
of spleen size

560
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:00,840
and how to quickly

561
00:25:00,840 --> 00:25:01,960
assess

562
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:03,680
for an enlarged

563
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:03,980
spleen

564
00:25:03,980 --> 00:25:05,020
on a coronal image.

565
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:06,580
So spleenomegaly

566
00:25:06,580 --> 00:25:07,400
